    "notes": "Now the key players in subrogation. First, insurance companies themselves. Many large insurers have their own subrogation departments or teams. So sometimes the lien letter really does come straight from the carrier. When that happens, you deal with the carrier's subrogation team directly, and you still need the same things: the itemized payments, a reference number, and the person handling the file."
