    "from": "hs-day4, slide 36",
    "handout": "",
    "notes": "Why does this rule exist? It is a safeguard so patients are not unfairly pursued for costs that should have been covered by Medicare or a third party, but were not properly handled by the provider. The same legal reference applies, 42 U.S.C. section 1395cc(a)(1). For our clients, this is protection: the provider's mistake in billing does not become the client's debt."
