    "from": "hs-day4, slide 39",
    "handout": "",
    "notes": "Third, the consequences. If the provider or hospital fails to bill Medicare within the twelve-month window, it cannot pursue the patient or the beneficiary for payment. The only exception is any deductibles or co-pays that apply under Medicare rules. So when a provider on a Medicare case is chasing the full bill well past a year, flag it for the attorney."
